  "id": "routing/a-chat-key-holding-no-chat-is-no-chat",
  "title": "A message whose chat key holds no value, or a value that is not a recipient, does not carry its chat: on WhatsApp Personal it is its sender's, on Telegram it has no address",
  "rules": [
    "§5.7",
    "§10.1 step 2",
    "§10.4"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-5.7-025",
    "RK-A.4-006",
    "RK-A.4-007"
  ],
  "notes": "Both channels take their type's addressing. No value: null, an empty or a blank string. Not a recipient: a boolean, a float, a whole one included, a list, an object. On WhatsApp Personal, whose replies go to the sender, each such message reaches its sender's room; the group id as a string is the group's. On Telegram, whose replies go to a chat only, each opens a room of its own naming the framework's name and no recipient (§10.4).",
